0	section	Talking with Launa to start
1	line	Player	Hi there.
1	line	Launa	Hello.
1	line	Player	What's this big hole in the ground all about?
1	line	Launa	Oh I wish I knew for sure... All I do know is that it opened seemingly by itself a few months ago. It was first discovered by the students over at the digsite, a few of which have gone down there but never returned.
1	line	Launa	They told me about it straight away.
1	line	Player	So why is it important to you?
1	line	Launa	A few reasons, but I think the situation is beyond help now.
1	line	Player	What situation? Maybe I can help.
1	line	Launa	I suppose it wouldn't hurt to tell you. I'm waiting to see my son Tolna. Don't suppose you've seen him?
1	line	Player	Your son, Tolna? I don't know, what does he look like?
1	line	Launa	I don't really know.
1	line	Player	You don't know what your own son looks like?
1	line	Launa	No. You see, I haven't seen him for... for... 25 years now. He just ran away one day and never returned. I'm hoping he's down this rift as I know he headed in this direction. My husband went to look, but he hasn't
1	line	Launa	returned for days.
1	select	Start the A Soul's Bane quest?
1	option	Yes
2	line	Player	Would you like me to go down to look for your husband and son?
2	line	Launa	You would do that? Oh thank you so much!
2	line	Player	Don't worry. I'll investigate.
2	line	Launa	Thank you. You can use a rope to get into the rift, just attach it at the edge.
2	line	Player	No problem.
2	line	Launa	Be careful.
2	action	end
1	option	No
2	line	Player	Surely by now they'd both be dead?
2	line	Launa	What?!?!
2	line	Player	Oops.
2	line	Launa	How could you say such a thing? Get away from me!
2	action	end
