0	section	Talking to human Tolna
1	line	Player	Tolna?
1	line	Tolna	Sorry? What happened?
1	line	Player	You've been trapped down here for years. I've come to rescue you on behalf of your parents.
1	line	Tolna	Oh yeah. I was looking for the legacy of a civilisation that used to live down here.
1	line	Brana	Son!
1	line	Tolna	Father? Oh, I'm so sorry, can you ever forgive me?
1	line	Brana	Don't worry, I'm just glad you're back to yourself. Are you OK?
1	line	Tolna	I'm fine, my memories are slowly returning. How's mother?
1	line	Brana	She misses you dearly!
1	line	Tolna	Where is she?
1	line	Player	She's up at the surface waiting for you.
1	line	Brana	Thank you traveller, I'm glad my wife and I never gave up hope. We should return to her and tell her the good news.
1	line	Tolna	Thank you so much. I truly owe you for your help.
1	line	Player	I'm just glad I could help.
1	action	end
1	action	The player is transported to above surface.
0	section	Talking to Tolna on the surface
1	line	Player	Hello Tolna.
1	line	Tolna	Hi. Thanks again for saving me, I'm so glad to be out of that horrible place. I was foolish to ignore my parents' warnings when I ran away that day. Luckily I've been able to patch things up with them so they've
1	line	Tolna	returned home with peace of mind.
1	line	Player	What exactly happened to you down there?
1	line	Tolna	I managed to find the remnants of the ancient civilisation that the stories talked about. It seems people used to worship a god there years ago in numbers far greater than a simple cult following. Sadly there is little
1	line	Tolna	remaining so I have nothing else to tell. As soon as I entered this area the ground swallowed me whole. I felt there was something watching, waiting. It's like there is some evil power under the ground that wanted me to
1	line	Tolna	suffer. As if it got some sort of empowerment from it. At least what ever it is, it doesn't want to reveal itself to the world yet...
1	line	Player	At least we have a warning. Did you manage to retrieve anything?
1	line	Tolna	Not really, just a few coins, which you're welcome to have.
1	line	Player	Thanks. So what are you going to do now?
1	line	Tolna	I've decided to keep open the rift. There is a part of it that is perfectly laid out for combat training and remnants of my subconscious remain in there. I want to show people the problems I have faced, so that they
1	line	Tolna	may learn from them. You're welcome to go down there and practice fighting any time.
1	line	Player	Thanks.
